---
/**
 * /why section 03: goals run in sprints. The sprint loop drawn large on the
 * void, the four-step lifecycle as a stepper, three comparisons that each use
 * a different device (A one large drawing, B red field, C split), and the
 * closing as a poster quote. Tasks are ASSIGNED by the
 * ScrumMaster (after an optional ask-protocol poll), never claimed off a
 * board. Long-form and diagram styles come from pages/why.astro.
 */
import SectionHead from './ui/SectionHead.astro';

interface Props {
  num?: string;
}

const { num = '03' } = Astro.props;

const compared = [
  { id: 'vs-goal-decomposition', letter: 'A', name: 'Goal Decomposition', systems: 'AutoGen · CrewAI · LangGraph' },
  { id: 'vs-cross-machine', letter: 'B', name: 'Cross-Machine Coordination', systems: 'OpenAI Swarm · Microsoft AutoGen · Anthropic MCP' },
  { id: 'vs-failure-recovery', letter: 'C', name: 'Failure & Recovery', systems: 'LangGraph · CrewAI · AutoGen' },
];
---

<section id="emergence" class="why-sec emergence-section">
  <div class="container">

    <SectionHead num={num} kicker="Sprints" title="Emergence">
      A team of agents plans the work in sprints and learns from what goes wrong.
    </SectionHead>

    <div class="poster">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="standfirst">
          Most agent setups decide the plan up front, before the first task runs. When the work doesn't match the plan, a person has to step in and rewrite it. Abject replaces the static plan with a <em>ScrumMaster</em> and sprints, inspired by Scrum. The ScrumMaster asks the team of agents what each one can do and hands out the sprint's tasks. Some agents think with an LLM and some just run code. When every task is done or failed, the ScrumMaster reviews what happened, failures included, and decides whether the goal is done, needs another sprint, or should stop. You describe what you want, not how to do it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <nav class="poster-side rindex" aria-label="Compared here">
        <p class="rindex-label">Compared here</p>
        <ol>
          {compared.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`#${c.id}`}>
                <span class="ri-n">{c.letter}</span>
                <span class="ri-t">{c.name}</span>
                <span class="ri-s">{c.systems}</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </nav>
    </div>

    <!-- The sprint loop, drawn large on the void -->
    <figure class="loop-hero">
      <p class="loop-label"><span class="sq" aria-hidden="true"></span>The sprint loop</p>
      <div class="fig-scroll">
        <svg class="dg loop-svg" viewBox="0 0 780 316" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="The sprint loop: a goal is created, the ScrumMaster asks the team of agents and plans a sprint, the assigned agents run the tasks, the ScrumMaster reviews the results, and the loop repeats until the goal is done">
          <defs>
            <marker id="sl-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path class="mk-live" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
            </marker>
            <marker id="sl-mk-dim" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path class="mk-live" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
            </marker>
          </defs>

          <!-- The goal, set by the human hand (or another abject) -->
          <rect class="n-key shadow" x="35" y="14" width="240" height="42"/>
          <text class="lbl t-key" x="155" y="41" text-anchor="middle">Goal: Build a dashboard</text>
          <text class="note note-i" x="292" y="40">created by you, or by another abject</text>
          <line class="ln-live" x1="155" y1="57" x2="155" y2="88" marker-end="url(#sl-mk)"/>

          <!-- Plan, Scrum, Review -->
          <rect class="n shadow" x="52" y="92" width="206" height="64"/>
          <text class="lbl" x="155" y="117" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Plan</text>
          <text class="note note-bone" x="155" y="135" text-anchor="middle">ScrumMaster asks the team:</text>
          <text class="note note-bone" x="155" y="148" text-anchor="middle">"can you? how?" then assigns</text>

          <line class="ln-live" x1="260" y1="124" x2="279" y2="124" marker-end="url(#sl-mk)"/>

          <rect class="n shadow" x="282" y="92" width="206" height="64"/>
          <text class="lbl" x="385" y="117" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Sprint</text>
          <text class="note note-bone" x="385" y="135" text-anchor="middle">assigned agents run tasks:</text>
          <text class="note note-bone" x="385" y="148" text-anchor="middle">some think, some just run code</text>

          <line class="ln-live" x1="490" y1="124" x2="509" y2="124" marker-end="url(#sl-mk)"/>

          <rect class="n shadow" x="512" y="92" width="206" height="64"/>
          <text class="lbl" x="615" y="117" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Review</text>
          <text class="note note-bone" x="615" y="135" text-anchor="middle">read the results,</text>
          <text class="note note-bone" x="615" y="148" text-anchor="middle">failures included</text>

          <!-- The team: tasks fan out from the scrum to their assigned agents -->
          <line class="ln-live-dim" x1="356" y1="157" x2="78" y2="194" marker-end="url(#sl-mk-dim)"/>
          <line class="ln-live-dim" x1="370" y1="157" x2="168" y2="194" marker-end="url(#sl-mk-dim)"/>
          <line class="ln-live-dim" x1="384" y1="157" x2="273" y2="194" marker-end="url(#sl-mk-dim)"/>
          <line class="ln-live-dim" x1="398" y1="157" x2="385" y2="194" marker-end="url(#sl-mk-dim)"/>
          <line class="ln-live-dim" x1="412" y1="157" x2="484" y2="194" marker-end="url(#sl-mk-dim)"/>

          <rect class="n shadow" x="40" y="198" width="72" height="30"/>
          <text class="id id-sm" x="76" y="217" text-anchor="middle">Chat</text>
          <rect class="n shadow" x="120" y="198" width="94" height="30"/>
          <text class="id id-sm" x="167" y="217" text-anchor="middle">WebAgent</text>
          <rect class="n shadow" x="222" y="198" width="102" height="30"/>
          <text class="id id-sm" x="273" y="217" text-anchor="middle">SkillAgent</text>
          <rect class="n shadow" x="332" y="198" width="108" height="30"/>
          <text class="id id-sm" x="386" y="217" text-anchor="middle">ObjectAgent</text>
          <rect class="n-dash" x="448" y="198" width="76" height="30"/>
          <text class="note note-bone" x="486" y="217" text-anchor="middle">+ yours</text>

          <text class="note note-i" x="282" y="248" text-anchor="middle">the standard team ships with every workspace;</text>
          <text class="note note-i" x="282" y="261" text-anchor="middle">add your own agents any time</text>

          <!-- Review -> Done -->
          <line class="ln-live" x1="665" y1="157" x2="665" y2="197" marker-end="url(#sl-mk)"/>
          <text class="note note-live note-i" x="673" y="182">complete</text>
          <rect class="n-live shadow" x="595" y="200" width="140" height="42"/>
          <text class="lbl t-live" x="656" y="226" text-anchor="middle">Goal done</text>
          <path class="ln-live" d="M 704 220 L 709 226 L 719 214" style="stroke-width:2"/>

          <!-- Loop back: Review -> Plan -->
          <path class="ln-live-dash" d="M 560 157 L 560 284 L 20 284 L 20 124 L 49 124" marker-end="url(#sl-mk)"/>
          <text class="note note-live note-i" x="291" y="304" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:11px">another sprint, as many as the work needs</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <p class="scroll-hint" aria-hidden="true">Scroll the diagram <span>&#9654;</span></p>
      <figcaption class="dg-cap loop-caps">
          <span class="cap-line">Every task is a tuple in TupleSpace, synced across peers.</span>
          <span class="cap-line">The review decides: finish the goal, plan another sprint, or stop.</span>
          <span class="cap-line">Learning happens when things go wrong. Failures feed the next sprint.</span>
        </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <!-- The lifecycle: four steps strung along one rule -->
    <ol class="stepper steps">
      <li>
        <span class="step-n" aria-hidden="true">I</span>
        <h3 class="step-title">Plan</h3>
        <p class="step-tagline">The ScrumMaster asks the team.</p>
        <p>You create a goal, or another abject does. The ScrumMaster picks it up, reads the goal, and recalls lessons from past goals. When it needs to know who can do what, it asks the team through the Ask Protocol: "Can you do this? How?" Each agent answers with an approach, or passes. Then the ScrumMaster hands out the sprint's tasks, each to the agent that fits it best.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="step-n" aria-hidden="true">II</span>
        <h3 class="step-title">Sprint</h3>
        <p class="step-tagline">Each agent works on its tasks.</p>
        <p>Every task is recorded as a tuple in TupleSpace, a last-writer-wins CRDT that syncs to the peers that subscribe to it, so the goal survives even if the machine it started on dies. Each task goes to the agent it was assigned to. Tasks that don't depend on anything start right away, and the rest start when the tasks they wait on finish. Some agents think with an LLM and some just run code.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="key">
        <span class="step-n" aria-hidden="true">III</span>
        <h3 class="step-title">Review</h3>
        <p class="step-tagline">The ScrumMaster reads what happened.</p>
        <p>When every task in the sprint is done or failed, the GoalManager emits <code>goalReadyForCompletion</code> and the ScrumMaster comes back. It reads what the sprint produced and what failed, then decides: finish the goal and write up the answer, plan another sprint, or fail the goal. There can be as many sprints as the work needs, and the plan is rewritten every time.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="step-n" aria-hidden="true">IV</span>
        <h3 class="step-title">Learn</h3>
        <p class="step-tagline">Learning happens when things go wrong.</p>
        <p>A failed task records its error, and the agent that hit it, in the goal's history. There is no retry budget. The next sprint reads the failure and decides what to do about it: add a task to fix it, give the work to a different agent, or stop. For each task, the agent predicts what the result should be. After the goal, those predictions are compared with what actually happened, and the lessons go into the KnowledgeBase, where later goals can find them. A GoalObserver also watches from outside and fails goals that go quiet for too long.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <!-- A: one large drawing on the void, the two texts beneath -->
    <article class="cmp" id="vs-goal-decomposition">
      <header class="cmp-head">
        <span class="cmp-letter" aria-hidden="true">A</span>
        <h3 class="cmp-title">Goal Decomposition</h3>
        <span class="cmp-systems">AutoGen &middot; CrewAI &middot; LangGraph</span>
      </header>
      <div class="bigdg">
        <svg class="dg" style="max-width: 520px" viewBox="0 0 380 168" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="A plan decided up front: one Orchestrator assigns work to three workers, which report back; one point of failure">
          <defs>
            <marker id="ea-l-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path class="mk-old" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
            </marker>
          </defs>
          <rect class="n-old shadow" x="110" y="10" width="160" height="38"/>
          <text class="lbl t-old-hi" x="190" y="35" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">Orchestrator</text>
          <text class="note" x="96" y="26" text-anchor="end">assigns</text>
          <text class="note note-i" x="284" y="26">reports back</text>
          <!-- assigns -->
          <line class="ln-old" x1="125" y1="48" x2="50" y2="88" marker-end="url(#ea-l-mk)"/>
          <line class="ln-old" x1="180" y1="48" x2="180" y2="88" marker-end="url(#ea-l-mk)"/>
          <line class="ln-old" x1="255" y1="48" x2="330" y2="88" marker-end="url(#ea-l-mk)"/>
          <!-- reports back -->
          <line class="ln-old-dash" x1="80" y1="92" x2="150" y2="51" marker-end="url(#ea-l-mk)"/>
          <line class="ln-old-dash" x1="200" y1="92" x2="200" y2="51" marker-end="url(#ea-l-mk)"/>
          <line class="ln-old-dash" x1="300" y1="92" x2="230" y2="51" marker-end="url(#ea-l-mk)"/>
          <!-- workers -->
          <rect class="n-old" x="6" y="92" width="110" height="34"/>
          <text class="lbl lbl-sm t-old" x="61" y="113" text-anchor="middle">Worker A</text>
          <rect class="n-old" x="135" y="92" width="110" height="34"/>
          <text class="lbl lbl-sm t-old" x="190" y="113" text-anchor="middle">Worker B</text>
          <rect class="n-old" x="264" y="92" width="110" height="34"/>
          <text class="lbl lbl-sm t-old" x="319" y="113" text-anchor="middle">Worker C</text>
          <text class="note note-i" x="190" y="158" text-anchor="middle">one planner, many workers, one point of failure</text>
        </svg>
        <div class="bigdg-div" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <svg class="dg" style="max-width: 520px" viewBox="0 0 380 292" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="A plan rewritten every sprint: the ScrumMaster plans each sprint into TupleSpace, agents watch and run their assigned tasks, and the plan is rewritten every sprint">
          <defs>
            <marker id="ea-r-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path class="mk-live" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
            </marker>
          </defs>
          <!-- TupleSpace, the shared record of the round -->
          <rect class="n shadow" x="90" y="105" width="200" height="56"/>
          <text class="id" x="190" y="129" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">TupleSpace</text>
          <rect x="158" y="139" width="10" height="10" style="fill:none; stroke: rgba(231,225,206,0.55); stroke-width:1.2"/>
          <rect x="176" y="139" width="10" height="10" style="fill:none; stroke: rgba(231,225,206,0.55); stroke-width:1.2"/>
          <rect class="fill-live" x="194" y="139" width="10" height="10"/>
          <rect x="212" y="139" width="10" height="10" style="fill:none; stroke: rgba(231,225,206,0.55); stroke-width:1.2"/>

          <!-- Chat -->
          <rect class="n shadow" x="6" y="10" width="110" height="36"/>
          <text class="id" x="61" y="33" text-anchor="middle">Chat</text>
          <line class="ln-live" x1="70" y1="48" x2="124" y2="103" marker-start="url(#ea-r-mk)" marker-end="url(#ea-r-mk)"/>
          <text class="note note-live" x="86" y="84" text-anchor="end">watch</text>

          <!-- WebAgent -->
          <rect class="n shadow" x="264" y="10" width="110" height="36"/>
          <text class="id" x="319" y="33" text-anchor="middle">WebAgent</text>
          <line class="ln-live" x1="310" y1="48" x2="256" y2="103" marker-start="url(#ea-r-mk)" marker-end="url(#ea-r-mk)"/>
          <text class="note note-live" x="294" y="84">run</text>

          <!-- ScrumMaster, the planner -->
          <rect class="n-key shadow" x="125" y="215" width="130" height="38"/>
          <text class="id t-key" x="190" y="239" text-anchor="middle">ScrumMaster</text>
          <line class="ln-live" x1="190" y1="213" x2="190" y2="163" marker-start="url(#ea-r-mk)" marker-end="url(#ea-r-mk)"/>
          <text class="note note-live" x="200" y="193">plan sprint</text>

          <!-- re-plan -->
          <path class="ln-live-dash" d="M 124 234 C 70 234 50 205 50 165 C 50 135 62 118 87 118" marker-end="url(#ea-r-mk)"/>
          <text class="note note-live" x="64" y="199">re-plan</text>

          <text class="note note-i" x="190" y="282" text-anchor="middle">one goal, one team, a new plan every sprint</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="bigdg-texts">
        <div>
          <p class="side-label">Them &middot; a plan decided up front</p>
          <p class="cmp-text">In AutoGen, a planner decides the order of the conversation and who speaks when. CrewAI gives crews fixed task pipelines that are set when you design them. LangGraph runs a state machine the developer draws before the system ever runs. In all of them the plan is decided before the first task starts, and it doesn't change.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="side-label hand">Abject &middot; a plan rewritten every sprint</p>
          <p class="cmp-text">A goal is planned in sprints. Each sprint, the ScrumMaster looks at what the last one produced, asks the team what each agent can do, and commits a new batch of assigned tasks to TupleSpace. Discovering something new in the middle of the work isn't treated as a defect in the plan. It's expected, and the next sprint plans around it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <!-- B: the red field, the diagrams in ink and bone -->
  <article class="cmp cmp-field field-red cut-top cut-bottom" id="vs-cross-machine">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="cmp-head">
        <span class="cmp-letter" aria-hidden="true">B</span>
        <h3 class="cmp-title">Cross-Machine Coordination</h3>
        <span class="cmp-systems">OpenAI Swarm &middot; Microsoft AutoGen &middot; Anthropic MCP</span>
      </header>
      <div class="field-pair">
        <div>
          <p class="fp-label ghosted">Them</p>
          <p class="fp-sub">one process</p>
          <svg class="dg" style="max-width: 360px" viewBox="60 20 300 140" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="One process: the agents are stuck inside one runtime process">
            <defs>
              <marker id="eb-l-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path class="mk-old" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <rect class="n-old shadow" x="70" y="28" width="250" height="100"/>
            <text class="head" x="195" y="47" text-anchor="middle">Runtime</text>
            <rect class="n-old" x="85" y="58" width="65" height="26"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-xs t-old" x="117" y="75" text-anchor="middle">Agent</text>
            <rect class="n-old" x="163" y="58" width="65" height="26"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-xs t-old" x="195" y="75" text-anchor="middle">Agent</text>
            <rect class="n-old" x="241" y="58" width="65" height="26"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-xs t-old" x="273" y="75" text-anchor="middle">Agent</text>
            <line class="ln-old" x1="150" y1="71" x2="162" y2="71" marker-end="url(#eb-l-mk)"/>
            <line class="ln-old" x1="228" y1="71" x2="240" y2="71" marker-end="url(#eb-l-mk)"/>
            <!-- the wall at the process boundary -->
            <line x1="320" y1="28" x2="320" y2="128" style="stroke: var(--diagram-muted); stroke-width: 4"/>
            <line class="ln-red" x1="332" y1="70" x2="344" y2="82"/>
            <line class="ln-red" x1="344" y1="70" x2="332" y2="82"/>
            <text class="note note-i" x="195" y="150" text-anchor="middle">agents stuck in one process</text>
          </svg>
          <p class="cmp-text">OpenAI Swarm runs its agents in one process and hands off between them, so the coordination stops at that process. AutoGen's multi-agent conversations also happen in one runtime. MCP connects tools across machines, but the agents stay local. The tools travel and the goals don't. None of them let agents on different machines work on the same goal without a central server holding the state.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="fp-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div>
          <p class="fp-label hand">Abject</p>
          <p class="fp-sub">peer to peer</p>
          <svg class="dg" style="max-width: 480px" viewBox="460 20 400 140" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Peer to peer: two peers each hold a TupleSpace kept in encrypted CRDT sync, and a worker on one peer works on a goal from the other">
            <defs>
              <marker id="eb-r-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path class="mk-live" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <!-- Peer A -->
            <rect class="n-frame shadow" x="470" y="28" width="150" height="90"/>
            <text class="head" x="545" y="45" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--bone-2)">Peer A</text>
            <rect class="n" x="485" y="53" width="120" height="27"/>
            <text class="id id-sm" x="545" y="71" text-anchor="middle">TupleSpace</text>
            <rect class="n" x="490" y="88" width="50" height="20"/>
            <text class="id" x="515" y="102" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:9.5px">Chat</text>
            <rect class="n" x="548" y="88" width="60" height="20"/>
            <text class="id" x="578" y="102" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:9.5px">Parser</text>

            <!-- Peer B -->
            <rect class="n-frame shadow" x="700" y="28" width="150" height="90"/>
            <text class="head" x="775" y="45" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--bone-2)">Peer B</text>
            <rect class="n" x="715" y="53" width="120" height="27"/>
            <text class="id id-sm" x="775" y="71" text-anchor="middle">TupleSpace</text>
            <rect class="n" x="730" y="88" width="84" height="20"/>
            <text class="id" x="772" y="102" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:9.5px">DataWorker</text>

            <!-- encrypted CRDT sync between the peers -->
            <line class="ln-live-dash" x1="620" y1="67" x2="715" y2="67"/>
            <rect class="fill-live" x="631" y="52" width="8" height="6"/>
            <path d="M 632.5 52 v -2.4 a 2.5 2.5 0 0 1 5 0 v 2.4" style="fill:none; stroke: var(--living); stroke-width: 1.2"/>
            <text class="note note-live" x="643" y="58" style="font-size:9.5px">CRDT sync</text>

            <!-- a worker on Peer B works on Peer A's goal -->
            <line class="ln-live-dash" x1="730" y1="98" x2="622" y2="75" marker-end="url(#eb-r-mk)"/>

            <text class="note note-bone note-i" x="660" y="150" text-anchor="middle">goals sync between peers, and any peer can do the work</text>
          </svg>
          <p class="cmp-text">Goals are CRDTs that sync between peers over encrypted WebRTC channels, with no central server. If a peer dies, the goal lives on every other peer that subscribed to it. The workers don't have to be LLM agents either. Any abject can register as a worker, including ones that just run code.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <div class="container">
    <!-- C: a split, the old way ghosted -->
    <article class="cmp" id="vs-failure-recovery">
      <header class="cmp-head">
        <span class="cmp-letter" aria-hidden="true">C</span>
        <h3 class="cmp-title">Failure &amp; Recovery</h3>
        <span class="cmp-systems">LangGraph &middot; CrewAI &middot; AutoGen</span>
      </header>
      <div class="split">
        <div class="ghost">
          <p class="side-label">Them <span class="sub">one failure breaks the chain</span></p>
          <svg class="dg" style="max-width: 440px" viewBox="30 30 370 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="One failure breaks the chain: one failed task kills every task after it">
            <defs>
              <marker id="ec-l-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path class="mk-old" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <rect class="n-old shadow" x="40" y="55" width="70" height="30"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-xs t-old" x="75" y="74" text-anchor="middle">Task</text>
            <line class="ln-old" x1="110" y1="70" x2="131" y2="70" marker-end="url(#ec-l-mk)"/>
            <rect class="n-old shadow" x="133" y="55" width="70" height="30"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-xs t-old" x="168" y="74" text-anchor="middle">Task</text>
            <line class="ln-old" x1="203" y1="70" x2="224" y2="70" marker-end="url(#ec-l-mk)"/>
            <!-- the failed task -->
            <rect class="n-fail shadow" x="226" y="55" width="70" height="30"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-xs t-red" x="261" y="74" text-anchor="middle">Task</text>
            <line class="ln-red" x1="300" y1="54" x2="312" y2="66"/>
            <line class="ln-red" x1="312" y1="54" x2="300" y2="66"/>
            <!-- everything after it is dead -->
            <rect class="n-dead" x="319" y="55" width="70" height="30"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-xs t-old" x="354" y="74" text-anchor="middle" style="opacity:0.45">Task</text>
            <text class="note note-i" x="215" y="115" text-anchor="middle">one failure kills the chain</text>
          </svg>
          <p class="cmp-text">LangGraph retries nodes, but the graph is fixed, so if the path is wrong, retrying the same node won't help. CrewAI's sequential pipelines break at the first failure. AutoGen's conversation chains stall when an agent can't respond. In all of them a failure moves forward through the plan and the plan doesn't change. Retrying harder with no memory of why it failed is a blind loop.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div>
          <p class="side-label hand">Abject <span class="sub">failures feed the next sprint</span></p>
          <svg class="dg" style="max-width: 440px" viewBox="484 24 356 136" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Failures feed the next sprint: a failed agent's error is recorded in TupleSpace, and the next sprint reassigns the task to another agent">
            <defs>
              <marker id="ec-r-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path class="mk-live" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
              </marker>
              <marker id="ec-r-mk-old" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path class="mk-old" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <!-- TupleSpace holds the task -->
            <rect class="n shadow" x="610" y="35" width="100" height="40"/>
            <text class="id id-sm" x="660" y="53" text-anchor="middle">TupleSpace</text>
            <rect x="641" y="61" width="7" height="7" style="fill:none; stroke: rgba(231,225,206,0.6); stroke-width:1"/>
            <text class="note" x="652" y="68" style="font-size:9.5px">task</text>

            <!-- the failed agent: its error is recorded -->
            <rect class="n-fail shadow" x="500" y="95" width="80" height="28"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-xs t-old" x="540" y="113" text-anchor="middle">Agent A</text>
            <line class="ln-red" x1="586" y1="98" x2="596" y2="108"/>
            <line class="ln-red" x1="596" y1="98" x2="586" y2="108"/>
            <line class="ln-old-dash" x1="540" y1="94" x2="628" y2="77" marker-end="url(#ec-r-mk-old)"/>
            <text class="note" x="496" y="78" style="font-size:9.5px">error recorded</text>

            <!-- the next sprint reassigns the work -->
            <rect class="n shadow" x="740" y="95" width="80" height="28"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-xs" x="780" y="113" text-anchor="middle">Agent B</text>
            <line class="ln-live" x1="780" y1="94" x2="702" y2="77" marker-end="url(#ec-r-mk)"/>
            <text class="note note-live" x="772" y="82" style="font-size:9.5px">reassigned</text>

            <text class="note note-bone note-i" x="662" y="118" text-anchor="middle">next sprint decides</text>
            <text class="note note-i" x="660" y="150" text-anchor="middle">the next sprint reads the failure</text>
          </svg>
          <p class="cmp-text">A failed task ends with its error written into the goal's history, and the sprint finishes around it. The next sprint reads that history and decides what to do: add a task to fix it, give the work to a different agent, or fail the goal. There is no fixed retry budget. A separate GoalObserver fails goals that go quiet for too long.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Closing: the poster quote -->
    <div class="closing">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="standfirst">It takes four pieces. A goal that you, or any abject, can create. A team the ScrumMaster can ask through the Ask Protocol. A shared TupleSpace that records every task and syncs it across peers. And a ScrumMaster that plans in sprints, reads what each sprint produced, failures included, and decides what to do next.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="poster-quote emergence-quote">A loop without memory is a treadmill. A loop with memory is a <em>ratchet.</em></p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Put the four pieces together and you get goals that survive the machine they started on, and plans that change after every sprint to route around what went wrong. Other frameworks decide the plan up front and hope it holds. Abject keeps planning until the work is done, and it remembers what it learned. It's too soon to tell how well this works at scale.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="defn"><span><em>emergence</em> (n.) - complex behavior that comes out of simple local interactions. Nobody conducts it.</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

